                            <comment id="495223" author="adilger" created="Thu, 28 May 2026 22:06:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;+119 failures in the past week.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ckansal&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ckansal&quot;&gt;ckansal&lt;/a&gt;, I see your patch is ready for review, but it is on you (and all developers) to seek out reviews for your patch.  A friendly ping once per week on a patch (sorted in priority) is useful to keep it moving forward.  Patches like this that fix intermittent failures should have a high priority since this affects all developers.  Doubly so for failures in sanity.sh since this runs 10x for every patch in different configurations, so even a 1% subtest failure has a 10% chance of affecting every version of every patch. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="495501" author="adilger" created="Fri, 5 Jun 2026 10:22:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;+130 failures in the past week.  Hopefully the fix will get into master-next and land soon...&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
